      "writtenOn": "2021-04-22T20:43:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had 2 requests:\n1. I think changing CONFIG_FLASH_FEATURE to CONFIG_FLASH_CROS or CONFIG_CROS_FLASH is more descriptive (e.g. this is a config for the Chromium EC code), but this is just a preference.\n2. Whatever name you settle on for the Chromium EC config name, the Kconfig name should always replace the CONFIG_ prefix with CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_.  For instance CONFIG_MY_NEW_OPTION becomes CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_MY_NEW_OPTION.  If you do this, you shouldn\u0027t need to add a new entry to config_allowed.txt.\n\nSo change the CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_FLASH to match your new config name (either CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_FLASH_FEATURE or CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_FLASH_CROS).",
